%description:

TcpCubic.fastConvergence:off -- at a loss below the previous W_max, W_max is the window at the loss.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "on a loss below the previous W_max, release extra window so a newly
arrived competing flow can grow (RFC 9438 section 4.7)".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false). The code: at a loss below the previous
W_max, fast convergence sets W_max = segCwnd * (1 + beta) / 2, else W_max = segCwnd
(TcpCubic::calculateSsthresh()). With beta 0.7 and the threshold beta * segCwnd, W_max over
the threshold is 0.85 / 0.7 = 1.21 with fast convergence and 1 / 0.7 = 1.43 without. This test separates "off" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic and without SACK, which sends 200000 bytes; the round
trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 15th and the 80th data segment once; the second loss
comes before the window regains its first W_max. Observation: level 3, at the second loss,
W_max over the new threshold is 1.43: no fast convergence.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.fastConvergence
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.fastConvergence
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicFastConvergenceOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 79 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 80th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .nth(2)
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.cubic_last_max_cwnd * 1448.0 / state.ssthresh >= 1.36 && state.cubic_last_max_cwnd * 1448.0 / state.ssthresh <= 1.6")
                  .describe("the threshold at the second loss, with W_max over it 1.43: no fast convergence")
                  .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicFastConvergenceOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.fastConvergence = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 200000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicFastConvergenceOff: PASS
